    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch09-19--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch09-19: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.26";
    dc:description "The passage states that no obvious mechanical account is available and points to fluid crystals as a direction in which to look, which does not fix variables or a decision rule. Adult skeletons show the polarity without showing where it was generated or which force class produced it. Existing images are compatible with the suggestion and with its rivals, so the claim as stated is not an empirical contrast.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: No outcome cleanly separates an unexplained central polarity, said to be perhaps like fluid-crystal directive forces, from other ways of placing a fixed set of spines. Locating the first sign of polarity in the central cytoplasm would address only that geographical clause.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Absence of an obvious mechanical force is not a measurement with a refuting result.", "Central origin, cortical origin and several molecular polarities can leave the same adult spine map.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.6"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.26"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch09-19--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of thompson1917-ch09-19 by Grok 4.7: 0.25";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
